                    "properties": {
                        "cwe": "CWE-502",
                        "severity": "High",
                        "reasoning": "The test constructs a serialized payload using SerializationHelper.toString(...) around a VulnerableTaskHolder that contains a command string (e.g., \"ping localhost -n 5\" or \"sleep 5\"). It then sends this payload as the value of the \"token\" parameter to the WebGoat lesson endpoint via checkAssignment(..., params, true). This is strong evidence that the lesson endpoint is expected to deserialize and then execute the embedded command, which is characteristic of insecure deserialization leading to command execution. Even though this is an integration test, the code demonstrates the exact mechanism by which a serialized object can carry and deliver an OS command through a client-controlled parameter.",
                        "mitigation": "Ensure the corresponding lesson implementation does not deserialize untrusted data (e.g., use a safe serialization format, disable polymorphic deserialization, and enforce allowlists). If deserialization is unavoidable, use strict type whitelisting and avoid any gadget classes that can lead to code execution. Additionally, never execute commands derived from deserialized content; use fixed server-side logic instead.",
