                        "severity": "Medium",
                        "reasoning": "If `MVNW_USERNAME`/`MVNW_PASSWORD` are set, the code installs a JVM-wide default `Authenticator` (line 101). Because the download URL is not validated (see other finding), any subsequent HTTP(S) requests made in the same JVM could reuse these credentials to authenticate to an attacker-controlled host. Even though this is a standalone downloader, the use of `setDefault` is still risky because it affects global state and can lead to credential leakage in the presence of other network operations.",
