                        "reasoning": "The endpoint accepts a userId directly from the request (@RequestParam String userId) and, upon successful verification, stores that same client-provided value into the session (userSessionData.setValue(\"account-verified-id\", userId)). There is no visible check that the authenticated/active user in the current LessonSession is the same as the provided userId, nor any authorization/ownership validation in this file. This pattern can enable an authentication/authorization bypass where an attacker supplies another user's ID and causes the session to be marked as verified for that ID.",
