                        "reasoning": "The controller uses a static mutable HashMap (votes) shared across all requests. In vote(), it performs a read-modify-write sequence (getOrDefault then put) without synchronization. Under concurrent requests, updates can be lost (classic race condition), and concurrent iteration/streaming over HashMap while it is being modified can lead to inconsistent results and, in some cases, runtime exceptions. Because these endpoints are public and likely accessed concurrently, this is a security-relevant integrity issue (data tampering via concurrency).",
