                        "cwe": "CWE-798",
                        "severity": "High",
                        "reasoning": "The endpoint /InsecureLogin/task accepts attacker-controlled request parameters (username, password) and performs authentication by directly comparing them to hardcoded string literals. Anyone who knows the literals can authenticate successfully without any real credential store, hashing, rate limiting, or session/token issuance. This is an authentication bypass vulnerability in practice (and is also the intended WebGoat lesson), because the server trusts client-supplied values and uses fixed secrets embedded in code.",
                        "mitigation": "Replace hardcoded credential checks with a proper authentication mechanism: store user credentials securely (e.g., salted password hashes in a database), verify using a password hashing function (e.g., BCrypt/Argon2), and implement standard auth/session handling. For a training app, at minimum avoid embedding real secrets in code and document that this is intentionally insecure for the lesson.",
