                        "cwe": "CWE-362",
                        "severity": "Medium",
                        "reasoning": "Refresh tokens are stored in a static, process-wide ArrayList. This is not thread-safe and can lead to race conditions (e.g., token reuse or inconsistent removal) under concurrent requests. Additionally, the code checks only whether the refresh token exists in the global list; it does not verify that the refresh token belongs to the same user as the access token claims. An attacker who obtains any valid refresh token could potentially use it with a different (but still signed) access token to mint new tokens for another user.",
                        "mitigation": "Use a thread-safe structure (e.g., ConcurrentHashMap) and store refresh tokens with associated user identity and expiration. Validate that the refresh token matches the user from the access token (or require only refresh-token-based identity). Consider persisting tokens with proper locking/atomic operations.",
