                        "mitigation": "Treat `username` as untrusted and encode/escape it according to the context where it will be used. If it is displayed in HTML, use proper HTML escaping (e.g., Spring's `HtmlUtils.htmlEscape` or a templating engine that auto-escapes) rather than manual `<br/>` insertion. If it is used for logging, log with structured logging (separate fields) and avoid concatenating/formatting untrusted strings into log lines. Also consider validating `username` against an allowlist of safe characters/length for this lesson.",
