                    "properties": {
                        "cwe": "CWE-639",
                        "severity": "High",
                        "reasoning": "The endpoint that performs the password change (`/PasswordReset/reset/change-password`) only verifies that the submitted `form.getResetLink()` exists in the global `resetLinks` list (lines 113-116). It does not enforce that the reset link belongs to the currently authenticated user (`@CurrentUsername username`). The ownership check (`checkIfLinkIsFromTom(...)`) is used only to decide whether to update `usersToTomPassword` (lines 117-119), but the method still returns the success view unconditionally (lines 120-121). As a result, any user who can obtain a valid reset link can submit it and reach the success state, and the code does not prevent unauthorized password reset attempts.",
                        "mitigation": "Enforce object-level authorization: after verifying `resetLinks.contains(...)`, also verify that the reset link is bound to the current user (or to a specific account) and reject the request if it is not. Concretely, make the `checkIfLinkIsFromTom(...)` (or a generalized ownership check) a required condition for proceeding; otherwise return an error view and do not indicate success. Additionally, store reset links with an associated user/account and expiry, and remove/consume links after use.",
