                        "cwe": "CWE-522",
                        "severity": "Medium",
                        "reasoning": "The controller accepts a user-provided \"secretKey\" from the request body and passes it directly into JWTToken.decode(...) and JWTToken.encode(...). While this may be intended for a WebGoat exercise, in a real application this pattern can lead to sensitive data exposure (the secret key is attacker-controlled and may be logged/returned by downstream code) and unsafe trust of client-controlled cryptographic material. Because the controller does not perform any validation, masking, or authorization checks around who can submit/receive secrets, the handling of secretKey is security-sensitive and currently unguarded at the controller level.",
