                    "properties": {
                        "cwe": "CWE-79",
                        "severity": "Medium",
                        "reasoning": "Backbone routes accept URL-controlled parameters (e.g., 'lesson/:name', 'lesson/:name/:pageNum', 'test/:param'). These parameters are passed directly to controller methods (loadLesson, updateMenu, testHandler) without any validation or encoding in this file. If any of those controller/view methods insert the values into the DOM (e.g., via innerHTML/templating without escaping), this can lead to DOM-based XSS. While the actual sink is not shown in this file, the lack of validation/encoding at the boundary is a security risk pattern for DOM XSS.",
                        "mitigation": "Validate and constrain route parameters at this boundary (e.g., allowlist lesson names, ensure pageNum is numeric, restrict test param to expected format). Additionally, ensure downstream views/controllers escape or safely render any user-controlled strings (use textContent/escaped templating rather than innerHTML).",
