                        "reasoning": "When `this.options.remote` is set, the modal loads remote content into `.modal-content` using jQuery `.load(url, ...)`. If `remote` can be influenced by an attacker (e.g., via `data-remote`/`data` attributes or untrusted configuration), this can cause the browser to fetch attacker-chosen URLs and inject the response into the DOM. While same-origin/CORS constraints apply, this still enables content injection and can be abused for XSS if the fetched content is attacker-controlled and executed in the page context.",
